<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pyotr Krasnov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1869–1947</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pyotr Krasnov was a Russian general and writer who led the anti-Bolshevik Don <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossacks</a> in 1918–1919 as ataman of the Almighty Don Host. With German support he raised a sizeable Don army and besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volgograd">Tsaritsyn</a>, but resigned in February 1919 after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s defeat. In exile he wrote popular novels and collaborated with Nazi Germany in raising Cossack units; handed over by the British, he was hanged in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> in 1947.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pyotr-krasnov.jpg" alt="Pyotr Krasnov" width="320" height="464" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pyotr_Nikolayevich_Krasnov.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
